{"step_index":168,"source":"MODEL","type":"GENERIC","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-16T00:46:52Z","content":"Created At: 2026-09-15T18:46:52-06:00\nCompleted At: 2026-09-15T18:46:52-06:00\nFile Path: `file:///C:/Users/djtwo/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/whisper_worship.txt`\nTotal Lines: 547\nTotal Bytes: 34276\nShowing lines 1 to 150\nThe following code has been modified to include a line number before every line, in the format: <line_number>: <original_line>. Please note that any changes targeting the original code should remove the line number, colon, and leading space.\n1: [00:04:42 -> 00:04:44] That's one of the things I love about our church.\r\n2: [00:04:44 -> 00:04:46] We come in with rejoicing, with excitement.\r\n3: [00:04:46 -> 00:04:48] We're not only excited to see each other,\r\n4: [00:04:48 -> 00:04:51] but above all, excited to see the Lord Jesus Christ here\r\n5: [00:04:51 -> 00:04:54] in our midst.\r\n6: [00:04:54 -> 00:04:59] The Psalmist said that we make a throne for God\r\n7: [00:04:59 -> 00:05:01] throughout praise.\r\n8: [00:05:01 -> 00:05:03] That's what we'd like to begin my singing,\r\n9: [00:05:03 -> 00:05:08] inviting the Lord to be enthroned in our praise.\r\n10: [00:05:08 -> 00:05:09] Think about that, dear brothers, dear sisters,\r\n11: [00:05:09 -> 00:05:14] that when we sing, when we truly praise\r\n12: [00:05:14 -> 00:05:16] from our hearts, without praise,\r\n13: [00:05:16 -> 00:05:17] comes from within our hearts,\r\n14: [00:05:17 -> 00:05:20] you're making a throne for the King of heaven,\r\n15: [00:05:20 -> 00:05:21] for the Lord of Lords.\r\n16: [00:05:21 -> 00:05:23] It's no light thing.\r\n17: [00:05:23 -> 00:05:25] If the King of the greatest King of this earth\r\n18: [00:05:25 -> 00:05:26] invited you to make a throne for him,\r\n19: [00:05:26 -> 00:05:29] think about the care and the joy\r\n20: [00:05:29 -> 00:05:30] with which you would do that.\r\n21: [00:05:30 -> 00:05:33] How much more the God of heaven,\r\n22: [00:05:33 -> 00:05:34] the King of Kings, the Lord of Lords,\r\n23: [00:05:34 -> 00:05:37] the only true King who's worthy to be exalted.\r\n24: [00:05:37 -> 00:05:39] Heavenly Father, I pray that this will be so\r\n25: \n<truncated 6817 bytes>\n 00:14:50] We live in a dark world in a world that's full of pain and hurt\r\n126: [00:14:50 -> 00:14:54] and hopelessness in a world of suicide,\r\n127: [00:14:54 -> 00:14:56] in a world of death, in a world of sorrow\r\n128: [00:14:56 -> 00:15:01] and broken relationships and divorce and family,\r\n129: [00:15:01 -> 00:15:04] disharmony, dysfunction.\r\n130: [00:15:04 -> 00:15:05] In the midst of that, there's one light\r\n131: [00:15:05 -> 00:15:10] that's one ray of hope and that is Jesus Christ alone.\r\n132: [00:15:10 -> 00:15:12] May we put our trust in Him today.\r\n133: [00:15:12 -> 00:15:17] May we afresh confess and proclaim that He alone is God.\r\n134: [00:15:17 -> 00:15:22] And He is the way, He is the truth, He is life.\r\n135: [00:15:22 -> 00:15:24] Come and trust Him afresh today, dear family.\r\n136: [00:15:24 -> 00:15:26] Come and put your faith afresh in Him.\r\n137: [00:15:26 -> 00:15:31] And say, Lord, I refuse to let to tie your hands through my unbelief.\r\n138: [00:15:31 -> 00:15:34] I refuse to limit your possibilities in my life\r\n139: [00:15:34 -> 00:15:36] anymore through unbelief.\r\n140: [00:15:36 -> 00:15:38] And I'm asking you, Lord, today, for that thing\r\n141: [00:15:38 -> 00:15:41] that I was afraid to ask you because it seemed hopeless.\r\n142: [00:15:41 -> 00:15:43] I'm asking you, today, Lord, to solve that problem\r\n143: [00:15:43 -> 00:15:46] that I've carried, that burden, that I've been carrying\r\n144: [00:15:46 -> 00:15:48] all this time, I laid at your feet and believe\r\n145: [00:15:48 -> 00:15:49] that you will untangle the knots.\r\n146: [00:15:49 -> 00:15:54] Jesus Christ came to untangle the knots of your life.\r\n147: [00:15:54 -> 00:15:55] And He will do that.\r\n148: [00:15:55 -> 00:15:57] He came.\r\n149: [00:15:57 -> 00:16:00] He came to destroy the works of the devil.\r\n150: [00:16:00 -> 00:16:02] And He's doing that.\r\nThe above content does NOT show the entire file contents. If you need to view any lines of the file which were not shown to complete your task, call this tool again to view those lines.\n","truncated_fields":["content"]}
