{"step_index":170,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-16T00:46:52Z","thinking":"The process completed successfully with 546 segments identified. Now, the structure of the data file is being examined to understand the distribution of audio segments. A Python script will be implemented to analyze the segments and classify them by content (e.g., singing versus talking).\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"write_to_file","args":{"ArtifactMetadata":"{\"RequestFeedback\":false,\"Summary\":\"Script to classify and print singing vs talking sections with exact timestamps\",\"UserFacing\":false}","CodeContent":"\"import json\\n\\ndef parse_time(sec):\\n    m, s = divmod(int(sec), 60)\\n    h, m = divmod(m, 60)\\n    return f\\\"{h:02d}:{m:02d}:{s:02d}\\\"\\n\\nwith open(r\\\"C:\\\\Users\\\\djtwo\\\\.gemini\\\\antigravity\\\\scratch\\\\whisper_worship.json\\\", \\\"r\\\", encoding=\\\"utf-8\\\") as f:\\n    segments = json.load(f)\\n\\nprint(f\\\"Total segments: {len(segments)}\\\")\\n\\n# Let's inspect intervals with gaps or distinct phrases\\nfor i, s in enumerate(segments):\\n    t_start = s[\\\"start\\\"]\\n    t_end = s[\\\"end\\\"]\\n    txt = s[\\\"text\\\"]\\n    # print sample lines every 15-20s or where big pauses occur\\n    if i > 0:\\n        prev_end = segments[i-1][\\\"end\\\"]\\n        gap = t_start - prev_end\\n        if gap > 8.0: # gap of silence or music without lyrics\\n            print(f\\\"--- GAP of {gap:.1f}s between {parse_time(prev_end)} and {parse_time(t_start)} ---\\\")\\n    \\n    # Print key lines\\n    print(f\\\"[{parse_time(t_start)} - {parse_time(t_end)}] {txt[:60]}\\\")\\n\"","Description":"\"Analyze gaps and transitions in segments\"","Overwrite":"true","TargetFile":"\"C:\\\\Users\\\\djtwo\\\\.gemini\\\\antigravity\\\\brain\\\\56930dde-d49e-4d64-b3a0-ddf3ad4cb3e8\\\\scratch\\\\identify_cuts.py\"","toolAction":"\"Create identify_cuts script\"","toolSummary":"\"Create identify_cuts.py\""}}]}
